Z||000000||fiero_hunter85||09-07-2001||09:23 AM||||i just got an 85 fiero GT that has been sitting since 1996. it has a bad leak in the windsheild and there are rust stains on the dash pad. i dont know how bad it is rusted yet but if it is bad will i have to replace the whole roof? or is there some other way to repair it?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||09-07-2001||10:21 AM||||I doubt the roof has rusted much, it's more common to find rust under the carpet up around the footwells because that's where the water would have sat the longest.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||09-07-2001||10:57 AM||||It's pretty easy to remove all the panels (+dash) around the windshield to see exactly where the water is travelling from.  If you have a sunroof, that would be the main suspect.  Mine had a leak at the top corner of the windscreen.  It actually may enter quite a ways from where the wet spots appear.<P>Gary||||reg||9
Z||000003||fiero_hunter85||09-07-2001||11:07 AM||||thanx for your reply's. i am going to take everything apart as soon as my dad gets the time to help me get it home today.||||reg||1
